node_modules/

# packages/ui/dist IS NOT IGNORED, and that is deliberate. Every consumer resolves this package
# through `link:../ui/packages/ui` — a symlink to this working tree — and no consumer runs a build
# here: not `pnpm install`, not the Dockerfiles (which COPY packages/ui out of a named build
# context), and not the second checkout in each frontend's CI. Committed output is therefore the
# only shape in which a built artefact reaches them at all. `src/dist.test.ts` recompiles the
# sources on every `pnpm test` and fails if a committed byte differs, so it cannot go stale
# unnoticed. See packages/ui/README.md, "Why the build output is in git".
#
# The parity test compiles into a sibling of dist/ — same depth, so a source map's relative
# `sources` entry comes out identical and the comparison measures the compiler rather than the
# path. It is removed when the test finishes; this line covers an interrupted run.
packages/*/.dist-check-*

*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
